SUMMARY:Finiteness and Density Problems for (Positive) Integral Points on M
 ordell–Schinzel Surfaces
DESCRIPTION:Séminaire de géométrie arithmétique In 1952\, Mordell erron
 eously claimed that the surface xyz = G(x\,y) has infinitely many integral
  points for any G ∈ ℤ [x\,y]. I will discuss a classification for fini
 teness and Zariski density of (positive) integral points on these log K3 s
 urfaces when the coefficients of G are non-negative. This combines a dynam
 ical argument proposed by Mordell\, the theory of…\nhttps://indico.math.
 cnrs.fr/event/17461/
